.TH MWM 1 mwm\-VERSION
.SH NAME
mwm \- matteo's window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mwm
.RB [ \-v ]
.RI [ \-c " FILE" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mwm
is a small dynamic tiling window manager for X. It manages windows in two
tiling layouts (equal columns and master+stack) plus floating, with
configurable gaps and optional rounded corners. Its CUI bar includes tags,
the focused title, root-window status, an XEmbed tray, an interactive calendar,
world clocks and a timer.
.PP
mwm has no built\-in keybindings. All control happens through the
.BR mwmc (1)
client over an X11 ClientMessage IPC channel, so keys are bound externally
(e.g. with sxhkd). Tags form one global pool shared across monitors; each tag
is owned by a single monitor and can be moved between monitors with its
windows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
print version information to stderr, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE"
read settings from FILE.
.TP
.B \-\-font-license
print the license for the bundled Geist fonts.
.SH USAGE
Start mwm from your
.B ~/.xinitrc :
.PP
.RS
.nf
exec mwm
.fi
.RE
.PP
Control it at runtime:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mwmc focus next
mwmc move win 3
mwmc layout stack
mwmc query state
.fi
.RE
.PP
See
.B mwmc help
for the full command grammar.
.SH CONFIGURATION
mwm reads
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mwm/config.ini
or
.B ~/.config/mwm/config.ini
and applies Xresources for appearance. Use
.B mwmc reload
to re-read both. The source includes an example in examples/config.ini.
.PP
After installing a replacement to the running mwm executable's path, use
.B mwmc restart
to load it in place and restore the existing session.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mwmc (1),
.BR sxhkd (1),
.BR slstatus (1),
.BR picom (1)
